---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends usage information to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink>. That covers app use,
      purchases, crashes, how well the app runs, and details about the app,
      device, and settings. Those details include accessibility settings, color
      scheme, language, layout direction, and region. We use all of it to see
      how people play and to make the app better.
    </p>
    <p>
      The app also makes a random ID for each install and sends a scrambled
      version of it. That ID stays the same until the app's data is reset or the
      app is deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics can be turned off in the app's settings. That stops new
      information from being sent. It does not delete what was already sent. We
      do not set a date for deleting old records, and those records have no name
      or email in them, so we cannot find one person's records to delete.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck has to protect this data at least as well as this policy and
      Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      A content report arrives as an email. It includes the reason, the round
      ID, the app version, and the build number. It is sent from the reporter's
      own email account, so we get that email address too. A drawing is included
      only if the reporter chooses to attach it. We use all of this to look into
      the report.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails stay in our support inbox. To have one deleted, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address it was sent from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track activity on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we make important changes to this policy, we will post them on this
      page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
